<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33417" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pălaestīnă</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pălest-</span></b> ),
			ae, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pă-laestīnē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παλαιστίνη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the country of Palestine</i>, <i>in
				Syria</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 11, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5,
				12, 13, § 66 sq.</span></i>—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pă-laestīnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Palestine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua,</span>”
				<i>the Euphrates</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					2, 464</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Syrus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					1, 8, 17</span></i>
			 (7, 18): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Palaestini simul Hebraeique liquores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 1, 213</span></i>
			. —In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pălaestīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Palestine</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4,
			46</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hier. in Isa. 14, 29</span></i>; <i>the Philistines</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen.
				21, 33</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pălaestīnensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>Palestinian</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Spart. Sev. 9</span></i>.</div>
